hib","kind":"person","brief":"Returned priest","count":1,"firstVerse":24},{"id":"shallum-h7967o","name":"Shallum","kind":"person","brief":"Returned divorcee","count":1,"firstVerse":24},{"id":"telem-h2928h","name":"Telem","kind":"person","brief":"Returned divorcee","count":1,"firstVerse":24},{"id":"uri-h0221i","name":"Uri","kind":"person","brief":"Returned divorcee","count":1,"firstVerse":24}],"places":[],"words":[{"base":"H4641","lemma":"מַעֲשֵׂיָהוּ","tr":"ma·a·se·yah","gloss":"Maaseiah","lang":"h","inPassage":3,"uses":23},{"base":"H3107","lemma":"יוֹזָבָד","tr":"yo·za·vad","gloss":"Jozacar","lang":"h","inPassage":2,"uses":11},{"base":"H0461","lemma":"אֱלִיעֶ֫זֶר","tr":"e·li·e·zer","gloss":"Eliezer","lang":"h","inPassage":2,"uses":14},{"base":"H4480","lemma":"מִן־","tr":"min","gloss":"from","lang":"h","inPassage":3,"uses":1187},{"base":"H2928","lemma":"טֶ֫לֶם","tr":"te·lem","gloss":"Telem","lang":"h","inPassage":1,"uses":2},{"base":"H0818","lemma":"אָשֵׁם","tr":"a·shem","gloss":"guilty","lang":"h","inPassage":1,"uses":3},{"base":"H3402","lemma":"יָרִיב","tr":"ya·riv","gloss":"Jarib","lang":"h","inPassage":1,"uses":3},{"base":"H7042","lemma":"קְלִיטָא","tr":"qe·li·ta","gloss":"Kelita","lang":"h","inPassage":1,"uses":3},{"base":"H6611","lemma":"פְּתַחְיָה","tr":"pe·tach·yah","gloss":"Pethahiah","lang":"h","inPassage":1,"uses":4},{"base":"H3136","lemma":"יוֹצָדָק","tr":"yo·tsa·daq","gloss":"Jozadak","lang":"h","inPassage":1,"uses":5}],"parallels":[],"crossrefs":[{"book":"LEV","chapter":6,"verse":6,"verseEnd":6,"votes":5,"source":"both","text":"Then he must bring to the priest his guilt offering to the LORD: an unblemished ram of proper value from the flock.","from":19},{"book":"LEV","chapter":5,"verse":15,"verseEnd":16,"votes":0,"source":"tsk","text":"“If someone acts unfaithfully and sins unintentionally against any of the LORDʼs holy things, he must bring his guilt offering to the LORD: an unblemished ram from the flock, of proper value in silver shekels according to the sanctuary shekel; it is a guilt offering. Regarding any holy thing he has harmed, he must make restitution by adding a fifth of its value to it and giving it to the priest, who will make atonement on his behalf with the ram as a guilt offering, and he will be forgiven.","from":19},{"book":"LEV","chapter":6,"verse":4,"verseEnd":4,"votes":0,"source":"tsk","text":"once he has sinned and becomes guilty, he must return what he has stolen or taken by extortion, or the deposit entrusted to him, or the lost property he found,","from":19},{"book":"LEV","chapter":21,"verse":7,"verseEnd":7,"votes":0,"source":"tsk","text":"A priest must not marry a woman defiled by prostitution or divorced by her husband, for the priest is holy to his God.","from":18},{"book":"LEV","chapter":21,"verse":13,"verseEnd":15,"votes":0,"source":"tsk","text":"The woman he marries must be a virgin. He is not to marry a widow, a divorced woman, or one defiled by prostitution. He is to marry a virgin from his own people, so that he does not defile his offspring among his people, for I am the LORD who sanctifies him.”","from":18},{"book":"1SA","chapter":2,"verse":22,"verseEnd":24,"votes":0,"source":"tsk","text":"Now Eli was very old, and he heard about everything his sons were doing to all Israel and how they were sleeping with the women who served at the entrance to the Tent of Meeting. “Why are you doing these things?” Eli said to his sons. “I hear about your wicked deeds from all these people. No, my sons; it is not a good report I hear circulating among the LORDʼs people.","from":18},{"book":"2KI","chapter":10,"verse":15,"verseEnd":15,"votes":0,"source":"tsk","text":"When he left there, he found Jehonadab son of Rechab, who was coming to meet him. Jehu greeted him and asked, “Is your heart as true to mine as my heart is to yours?” “It is!” Jehonadab replied. “If it is,” said Jehu, “give me your hand.” So he gave him his hand, and Jehu helped him into his chariot,","from":19},{"book":"1CH","chapte